<p>Ye, the US rapper formerly known as Kanye West, said he had postponed a concert scheduled for June in Marseille after the UK blocked him from entering the country and French authorities weighed whether to stop the show from going ahead. The planned Marseille performance had become a political issue in France, where local and national officials were considering whether to let it proceed.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/grm94kB4sP5ygpSTmlQy0xA-GkVPRcquJEWoVqGRnpOoh6uNHiIq4D1uaTAGsO8tIdWtapvKR4Sx8Wlr-pkiIg09jjRleFwYAAU_-UEystg-PN3gy3kiDPVFeGdGKbTWac5Bz5Vo7T1pmW4MJHpoHY498tzbNdA1CWwLRliuLA0' alt='Ye announced that he had postponed a concert in Marseille, France.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Timing: BBC said the postponement came about a week after the UK government announced it would block West from entering the country.</li><li>UK spillover: DW said the entry refusal also canceled West’s planned headline appearance at Wireless Festival.</li><li>Broader controversy: Le Monde said the debate in France pointed not only to West’s antisemitic remarks but also to his voiced admiration for Adolf Hitler.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Marseille mayor Benoît Payan: He said he did not want the city to become &quot;a showcase for those who promote hatred,&quot; making clear his opposition to the concert. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/europe/kanye-west-ye-france-concert.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c36rrrp5wnlo'>Kanye West postpones France gig following UK ban</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/europe/kanye-west-ye-france-concert.html'>Kanye West Postpones Concert in France as Government Considers Banning It</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/kanye-west-postpones-france-concert-after-uk-visa-denial/a-76785732'>Kanye West postpones France concert after UK visa denial</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='http